      "description": "Watch Watford vs Crawley Town highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. Under the lights of the Carabao Cup , Watford and Crawley Town locked horns in a clash that tested the nerves and endurance of both squads. Fans were treated to a night of persistent attacks and defensive heroics that kept the outcome uncertain until the very last moments. Early Battles and Goalkeeping Heroics On August 8, 2026 , the Carabao Cup stage was set for a tense encounter. From the opening whistle, Watford looked to assert dominance, with Iker Bravo testing Vito Mannone as early as the 3rd minute. The Crawley Town goalkeeper was kept busy throughout the first half, notably denying Othmane Maamma twice in a frantic 7th minute. Despite the pressure, the visitors held firm, occasionally venturing forward as Stephen Duke-McKenna forced a save from Federico Ravaglia around the half-hour mark. Second Half Drama and Woodwork Rattled The intensity ramped up after the break. Watford introduced Amin Nabizada , who immediately made an impact by setting up Iker Bravo , only for the shot to whistle wide. The most agonising moment for the home side came in the 60th minute when Luca Kjerrumgaard saw his effort strike the left post. As the clock ticked down, a flurry of yellow cards for players like Charlie Barker and Kellan Gordon showed the rising tension, while injuries to Gianmarco Di Biase and Othmane Maamma disrupted the flow of the match. The Decisive Blow in Added Time With nine minutes of stoppage time announced, the match seemed destined for a stalemate. However, in the 99th minute, the deadlock was finally shattered. Rocco Vata found Marc Bola outside the area, and the defender unleashed a spectacular right-footed strike into the top left corner. This late breakthrough proved to be the difference, as Watford navigated the final seconds of the 12 added minutes to secure their progression in the tournament."
